# Super Dodge Ball (USA) - "bean ball run" input schedule.
#
# RECORDED, not written. Captured with `nes_game --record-input` (or
# `tools/play_record.sh`) by playing the game, in game mode BEAN BALL, then
# running across the full map. Kept because the Bean Ball sprite-list
# degeneration (research.md 26, plan.md item 14) needs a run in that mode, and
# no hand-written schedule reproduces it: the camera has to travel the whole map
# while the player is moving, and the failure is in how the flicker mod's sprite
# list behaves while it happens.
#
# The bug is OPEN and UNATTRIBUTED - it is not known yet whether the game emits
# fewer sprites in this mode or the mod drops them, and those need opposite fixes.
# Replay it in a WINDOW, not headless: the window and the headless host do not
# run the same guest state (frames 0-3 match, frame 4 diverges -- research.md 26).
# A --virtual-pad replay also needs Player1Source = 2, because player 1 is the
# keyboard and player 2 the controller.
#
# Symptom to look for: the presented sprite list shrinks as the run proceeds
# (SDB_TRACE=1 prints `sdb <frame> <peak-list> ...` per frame), ending with one
# player sprite cut in half. Compare against the committed stadium vectors, which
# sit at 44-54 throughout.
#
# Format: one "<frame> <BUTTONS>" line per state change, absolute state
# ("-" is release). `#` starts a comment.
